<title>USA: IVI has enough cash to fund operations.</title>
<headline>IVI has enough cash to fund operations.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>IVI Publishing Inc said Monday it ended 1996 with a cash position of $3.5 million, which it continues to believe is sufficient to fund its operations.</p>
<p>The company, an electronic publisher of interactive multimedia health and medical information, reported a fourth-quarter loss of $2.1 million or $0.28 per share. Results included a $289,000 charge related to an arbitration award, which the company said it expects eventually will be reduced in the court confirmation process.</p>
<p>For the full year, IVI posted a loss of $1.36 per share.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
